A Client requests a deep cleaning service to prepare their home.
A Client updates an existing booking to include window cleaning for an upcoming event.

A Service Coordinator reviews a new cleaning request to determine staffing and time requirements.
A Service Coordinator schedules a cleaning team for a confirmed booking to ensure proper coverage.

A Cleaning Staff member gathers the required cleaning supplies before heading to the job site.
A Cleaning Staff member performs the scheduled cleaning tasks to meet the client’s expectations.
A Cleaning Staff member reports a supply shortage to ensure future jobs remain stocked.

A Quality Inspector reviews the completed cleaning work to verify that standards are met.
A Quality Inspector documents any issues found during inspection to guide corrections.
A Quality Inspector confirms the job as complete so the client can be notified of the finished service.

A Supply Clerk receives a report about a supply shortage.
A Supply Clerk makes an order for new supply, so the inventory has enough stock.
A Supply Clerk manages and monitors the inventory to make sure all supplies are up to standard.